01C1.2332 0.621633 1.07204 0.624355 0.911523 0.625391C0.832415 0.625899 0.754223 0.625812 0.688867 0.624414C0.654372 0.623674 0.622217 0.620283 0.595117 0.618555Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.1"/>
      </svg>
        <span class="acl__filter-label">{{ section.settings.trigger_label | escape }}</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="page-width acl__row">
    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A list of links to collections, which is what a `<nav>` is for. Not a
        tablist: these are addresses, they work as addresses without the
        script, and calling them tabs would promise a keyboard behaviour —
        arrow keys moving between them — that real links do not have.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav
        class="acl__list{% if section.settings.sticky_list %} acl__list--sticky{% endif %}"
        aria-label="{{ section.settings.list_label | escape }}"
      >
        <ul class="acl__items" role="list">
          {%- comment -%}
            Three kinds of row, and the type decides which. A `collection` is a
            tab as it always was. A `group` is a heading with nothing behind it —
            "Concerns" names the concerns rather than being one, so it is a label
            and not a link. A `concern` is one of the things under it.

            The group opens a nested list and the concerns after it fall into
            that list until the next group closes it. That nesting is not
            decoration: a screen reader reading the rail should hear that these
            seven are a set belonging to a name, which `aria-labelledby` on the
            sub-list is what says.

            A concern placed before any group has nowhere to belong, so it is
            rendered on its own rather than dropped — a merchant reordering
            blocks should never see one silently vanish.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign in_group = false -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign block_collection = block.settings.collection
              assign label = block.settings.label
              if label == blank
                assign label = block_collection.title
              endif
              assign is_active = false
              if forloop.index0 == active_index
                assign is_active = true
              endif
            -%}

            {%- case block.type -%}
              {%- when 'group' -%}
                {%- if in_group -%}
                      </ul>
                    </details>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign group_open = section.settings.groups_open
                  if block.id == active_group
                    assign group_open = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <li class="acl__item acl__item--group" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    A `<details>`, the same as the FAQ's questions and the contact
                    page's. The browser owns opening it, the keyboard behaviour
                    and telling a screen reader whether it is open — none of which
                    is worth reimplementing, and all of which keeps working with
                    the script switched off.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <details class="acl__disclosure"{% if group_open %} open{% endif %}>
                    <summary class="acl__group" id="acl-group-{{ block.id }}">
                      <span class="acl__group-text">{{ label }}</span>
                      <span class="acl__caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    </summary>
                    <ul class="acl__children" role="list" aria-labelledby="acl-group-{{ block.id }}">
                {%- assign in_group = true -%}

              {%- when 'concern' -%}
                {%- if block_collection != blank -%}
                  <li class="acl__child{% unless in_group %} acl__child--loose{% endunless %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <a
                      class="acl__childlink{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
                      href="{{ block_collection.url }}"
                      data-acl-link
                      data-acl-handle="{{ block_collection.handle }}"
                      {% if is_active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                    >
                      {%- comment -%}
                        The box is drawn, not an input. Only one concern is open
                        at a time, so a real checkbox would promise a choice the
                        rail does not offer — and this is a link, which is what
                        lets it work with the script switched off.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="acl__childlabel">{{ label }}</span>
                      {%- if section.settings.show_count -%}
                        <span class="acl__childcount">({{ block_collection.all_products_count }})</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}

              {%- else -%}
                {%- if in_group -%}
                      </ul>
                    </details>
                  </li>
                  {%- assign in_group = false -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block_collection != blank -%}
                  <li class="acl__item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <a
                      class="acl__link{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
                      href="{{ block_collection.url }}"
                      data-acl-link
                      data-acl-handle="{{ block_collection.handle }}"
                      {% if is_active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                    >
                      <span class="acl__label">{{ label }}</span>
                      {%- if section.settings.show_count -%}
                        {%- comment -%}
                          Every tab carries its count, but only the open one
                          shows it — the stylesheet decides that, not the
                          script. So the number follows the selection on its own,
                          and the list never has to be re-rendered to keep up
                          with the grid.

                          Padded to two figures below ten, which is how it is
                          drawn: a lone digit floating beside a word reads as a
                          typo rather than a total.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        {%- assign count = block_collection.all_products_count -%}
                        <sup class="acl__count">
                          {%- if count < 10 -%}0{%- endif -%}{{ count }}
                        </sup>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if in_group -%}
                </ul>
              </details>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Availability and sort are not collections, so they are not blocks —
            there is nothing for a merchant to choose. They are the same
            disclosure the concerns sit in, so the rail has one way of asking a
            question rather than three.

            Every row is a real link carrying the whole state in its URL. That
            is what makes the rail work with the script switched off, and it is
            what the script reads when it is on.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section.settings.show_availability -%}
            {%- assign base = collection.url | default: '/collections/all' -%}
            <li class="acl__item acl__item--group">
              <details class="acl__disclosure"{% if cur_avail != '' %} open{% endif %}>
                <summary class="acl__group" id="acl-avail-{{ section.id }}">
                  <span class="acl__group-text">{{ section.settings.availability_label | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="acl__caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </summary>
                <ul class="acl__children" role="list" aria-labelledby="acl-avail-{{ section.id }}">
                  <li class="acl__child">
                    <a class="acl__childlink{% if cur_avail == '1' %} is-active{% endif %}"
                       href="{{ base }}?filter.v.availability=1"
                       data-acl-facet="availability" data-acl-value="1"
                       {% if cur_avail == '1' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                      <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="acl__childlabel">{{ section.settings.in_stock_label | escape }}</span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                  <li class="acl__child">
                    <a class="acl__childlink{% if cur_avail == '0' %} is-active{% endif %}"
                       href="{{ base }}?filter.v.availability=0"
                       data-acl-facet="availability" data-acl-value="0"
                       {% if cur_avail == '0' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                      <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="acl__childlabel">{{ section.settings.out_of_stock_label | escape }}</span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </details>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_sort and collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
            {%- assign base = collection.url | default: '/collections/all' -%}
            <li class="acl__item acl__item--group">
              <details class="acl__disclosure">
                <summary class="acl__group" id="acl-sort-{{ section.id }}">
                  <span class="acl__group-text">{{ section.settings.sort_label | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="acl__caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </summary>
                <ul class="acl__children" role="list" aria-labelledby="acl-sort-{{ section.id }}">
                  {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                    <li class="acl__child">
                      <a class="acl__childlink{% if option.value == cur_sort %} is-active{% endif %}"
                         href="{{ base }}?sort_by={{ option.value }}"
                         data-acl-facet="sort" data-acl-value="{{ option.value }}"
                         {% if option.value == cur_sort %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                        <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="acl__childlabel">{{ option.name | escape }}</span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </details>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      `aria-live` on the grid rather than on anything around it: the swap is
      the only thing on the page that changes without the page moving, so this
      is what has to announce itself. `aria-busy` covers the wait in between.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="acl__panel" data-acl-panel>
      <ul
        class="acl__grid grid product-grid grid--{{ section.settings.columns_mobile }}-col-tablet-down grid--{{ section.settings.columns_desktop }}-col-desktop"
        id="acl-grid-{{ section.id }}"
        data-acl-grid
        aria-live="polite"
        aria-busy="false"
      >
        {%- if active_collection != blank -%}
          {% render 'all-collections-grid', grid_collection: active_collection, section_id: section.id %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- if section.settings.mobile_drawer -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The same collections the rail lists, presented the way a phone can carry
      them: a list of groups, each opening onto its own options. A `<dialog>`,
      so the focus trap, the escape key and the inertness of everything behind
      it are the browser's job rather than ours.

      Choosing here does not navigate. It stages a choice, and APPLY hands it to
      the rail link that already knows how to fetch that collection — so the
      drawer adds a way to choose and nothing else. Turn the setting off and the
      page is exactly what it was.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <dialog class="acl__drawer" data-acl-drawer aria-labelledby="acl-drawer-title-{{ section.id }}">
      <div class="acl__drawer-inner">
        <header class="acl__drawer-head">
          <div class="acl__drawer-titles">
            <p class="acl__drawer-title" id="acl-drawer-title-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.drawer_label | escape }}</p>
            <p class="acl__drawer-count" data-acl-drawer-count></p>
          </div>
          <button class="acl__drawer-close" type="button" data-acl-drawer-close aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 27 27" width="27" height="27" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <circle cx="13.5" cy="13.5" r="13.5" fill="#e6e6e6"/>
              <path d="M9.5 9.5l8 8M17.5 9.5l-8 8" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </header>

        <div class="acl__drawer-body">
          {%- comment -%}
            The list of groups. "Category" is the tabs themselves, which have no
            block of their own to name them — every other group is a `group`
            block and names itself.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ul class="acl__sheet" role="list" data-acl-sheet="root">
            <li class="acl__sheet-item">
              <button class="acl__grouprow" type="button" data-acl-goto="category">
                <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.category_label | escape }}</span>
                <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              </button>
            </li>
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'group' -%}
                <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                  <button class="acl__grouprow" type="button" data-acl-goto="{{ block.id }}">
                    <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</span>
                    <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if section.settings.show_availability -%}
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__grouprow" type="button" data-acl-goto="availability">
                  <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.availability_label | escape }}</span>
                  <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.show_sort and collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__grouprow" type="button" data-acl-goto="sort">
                  <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.sort_label | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="acl__grouprow-value" data-acl-sort-value></span>
                  <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>

          {%- comment -%}
            One sheet per group. The first row of each is the group's own name
            and goes back — the design draws it as a row like any other, and it
            is the only way back on a screen with no room for a title bar.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ul class="acl__sheet" role="list" data-acl-sheet="category" hidden>
            <li class="acl__sheet-item">
              <button class="acl__backrow" type="button" data-acl-back>
                <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.category_back_label | escape }}</span>
                <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 10H4M9 5l-5 5 5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              </button>
            </li>
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'collection' and block.settings.collection != blank -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign opt_label = block.settings.label
                  if opt_label == blank
                    assign opt_label = block.settings.collection.title
                  endif
                -%}
                <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                  <button class="acl__optionrow" type="button" data-acl-option data-acl-facet="collection" data-acl-value="{{ block.settings.collection.handle }}" data-acl-handle="{{ block.settings.collection.handle }}">
                    <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="acl__optionlabel">{{ opt_label | escape }}</span>
                    <span class="acl__optioncount">({{ block.settings.collection.all_products_count }})</span>
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>

          {%- assign sheet_open = false -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- case block.type -%}
              {%- when 'group' -%}
                {%- if sheet_open -%}</ul>{%- endif -%}
                <ul class="acl__sheet" role="list" data-acl-sheet="{{ block.id }}" hidden>
                  <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                    <button class="acl__backrow" type="button" data-acl-back>
                      <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</span>
                      <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 10H4M9 5l-5 5 5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                {%- assign sheet_open = true -%}
              {%- when 'concern' -%}
                {%- if sheet_open and block.settings.collection != blank -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign opt_label = block.settings.label
                    if opt_label == blank
                      assign opt_label = block.settings.collection.title
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                    <button class="acl__optionrow" type="button" data-acl-option data-acl-facet="collection" data-acl-value="{{ block.settings.collection.handle }}" data-acl-handle="{{ block.settings.collection.handle }}">
                      <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="acl__optionlabel">{{ opt_label | escape }}</span>
                      <span class="acl__optioncount">({{ block.settings.collection.all_products_count }})</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if sheet_open -%}</ul>{%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_availability -%}
            <ul class="acl__sheet" role="list" data-acl-sheet="availability" hidden>
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__backrow" type="button" data-acl-back>
                  <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.availability_label | escape }}</span>
                  <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 10H4M9 5l-5 5 5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
              </li>
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__optionrow" type="button" data-acl-option data-acl-facet="availability" data-acl-value="1" aria-pressed="false">
                  <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="acl__optionlabel">{{ section.settings.in_stock_label | escape }}</span>
                </button>
              </li>
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__optionrow" type="button" data-acl-option data-acl-facet="availability" data-acl-value="0" aria-pressed="false">
                  <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="acl__optionlabel">{{ section.settings.out_of_stock_label | escape }}</span>
                </button>
              </li>
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_sort and collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
            <ul class="acl__sheet" role="list" data-acl-sheet="sort" hidden>
              <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                <button class="acl__backrow" type="button" data-acl-back>
                  <span class="acl__grouprow-label">{{ section.settings.sort_label | escape }}</span>
                  <svg class="acl__rowarrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 10H4M9 5l-5 5 5 5" stroke="#33363F" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
              </li>
              {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                <li class="acl__sheet-item">
                  <button class="acl__optionrow" type="button" data-acl-option data-acl-facet="sort" data-acl-value="{{ option.value }}" aria-pressed="false">
                    <span class="acl__box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="acl__optionlabel">{{ option.name | escape }}</span>
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <footer class="acl__drawer-foot">
          <span class="acl__drawer-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="acl__drawer-actions">
            <button class="acl__apply" type="button" data-acl-apply>{{ section.settings.apply_label | escape }}</button>
            <button class="acl__clear" type="button" data-acl-clear>{{ section.settings.clear_label | escape }}</button>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "All Collections",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-all-collections",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "offset_header",
      "label": "Start below the header",
      "info": "Turn on when this is the first section on the page. The site header floats over the page until it is scrolled, so the first section has to hold its own content clear of it.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "list_position",
      "label": "List position",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "left",
          "label": "Left"
        },
        {
          "value": "right",
          "label": "Right"
        }
      ],
      "default": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "list_width",
      "min": 120,
      "max": 360,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "List width",
      "default": 200
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "column_gap",
      "min": 16,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Space between list and products",
      "default": 56
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Background",
      "default": "#FFFFFF"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Collection list"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "list_label",
      "label": "List description",
      "info": "Read out in place of the list by a screen reader. Not shown on the page.",
      "default": "Collections"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "sticky_list",
      "label": "Keep the list in view while the products scroll",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "sticky_gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Gap the held list keeps",
      "info": "How far the list stays clear of the site header, and of the top of the screen once the header has scrolled away.",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_count",
      "label": "Show the product count",
      "info": "Shown beside the open collection only.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "groups_open",
      "label": "Open groups by default",
      "info": "A group opens on its own anyway whenever one of its concerns is the collection being shown.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "item_gap",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Space between collections",
      "default": 14
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "list_color",
      "label": "Collection name colour",
      "default": "#4A4A4A"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "list_active_color",
      "label": "Open collection colour",
      "default": "#0A0A0B"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Products"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Columns on desktop",
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grid_gap_horizontal",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Space between columns",
      "info": "This grid only. The rest of the store keeps the spacing set in Theme settings.",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grid_gap_vertical",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 80,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Space between rows",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "columns_mobile",
      "label": "Columns on mobile",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1",
          "label": "1 column"
        },
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "2 columns"
        }
      ],
      "default": "2"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding top",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding bottom",
      "default": 72
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Phone filter drawer",
      "info": "Below 990px the rail becomes a drawer, opened by a button above the products."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "mobile_drawer",
      "label": "Use a drawer on phones",
      "info": "Off leaves the row of tabs that scrolls sideways.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "trigger_label",
      "label": "Filter bar text",
      "info": "The strip on phones that opens the drawer.",
      "default": "FILTERS AND SORT"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "drawer_label",
      "label": "Drawer title",
      "default": "FILTER AND SORT"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "category_label",
      "label": "Name for the collection tabs",
      "info": "The tabs have no block of their own to name them, so they are named here.",
      "default": "Category"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "category_back_label",
      "label": "Collection tabs — heading inside the drawer",
      "default": "By Category"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "apply_label",
      "label": "Apply button",
      "default": "APPLY"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "clear_label",
      "label": "Clear link",
      "default": "Clear"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_availability",
      "label": "Show availability",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "availability_label",
      "label": "Availability heading",
      "default": "Availability"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "in_stock_label",
      "label": "In stock label",
      "default": "In stock"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "out_of_stock_label",
      "label": "Out of stock label",
      "default": "Out of stock"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_sort",
      "label": "Show sort",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sort_label",
      "label": "Sort heading",
      "default": "Sort by"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "name": "Collection",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "collection",
          "id": "collection",
          "label": "Collection"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Name",
          "info": "Optional — what to call it in the list. Falls back to the collection's own title."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "group",
      "name": "Group heading",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "A name for the rows under it — \"Concerns\" — with no collection of its own. Every Concern block after this one belongs to it, until the next heading."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Concerns"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "concern",
      "name": "Concern",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One concern, under the heading above it. Opens its own collection, the same as a tab does."
        },
        {
          "type": "collection",
          "id": "collection",
          "label": "Collection"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label",
          "info": "Leave blank to use the collection's own title."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "All Collections"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
